# я and ю sit on two foreign latin-1 letter bytes -- ð and þ -- that survive the
# is-letter filter and reach generate_ital_diaphons but that Italian has no
# working arm for (proven: ð fell into the dental arm, þ dropped). Neither is
# reachable by the LATE own-test the way the accented block c0-de is, so instead
# pol_test_own_letters is HOISTED to the front of generate_ital_diaphons (see
# it_phone.dr) where it runs before every Italian arm and catches these two -- and
# every other Cyrillic letter -- regardless of byte.
